CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ head0 == a: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ head1 == b: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
A variadic constructor whose trailing parameter pack is empty in the recursion
base expands the pack to zero parameters and initializes each subobject,
mirroring the libstdc plus plus _Tuple_impl recursive constructor for a
two-element tuple.  The recursion base TImpl with an empty Tail expands the
constructor parameter pack to no parameters and collapses the empty-pack base
initializer, so construction succeeds and the head subobjects are initialized.
